    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.tabline\n\n### Description\n\nI'd like to see underline indicator for current active buffer as following\r\n\r\n<img width=\"481\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2022-11-06 at 11 26 31 am\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1514823/200148446-d06c8e78-62fe-48be-9dc4-db63a433b05f.png\">\r\n\r\nAt the moment, I'm using akinsho/bufferline.nvim with custom `TablineSel` highlight group to get the above look. To be honest, I prefer your plugin because `bufferline.nvim` is more feature-bloated, and I don't use all of them.\r\n\r\nThank you for great plugin!",
